<b>Miura</b>

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:31.330
<b>Kouda</b>

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:31.330
<b>Yamamuro</b>

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.430
<i>First base, Haneda-kun.</i>

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.330
<b>Seko</b>

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:31.790
<i>Second base, Idemitsu-kun.</i>

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:34.220
<i>Third base, Hayasaka-kun.</i>

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.420
<i>Shortstop, Mayumura-san.</i>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.630
<b>Miura</b>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.510
<b>Uozumi</b>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.510
<b>Hayasaka</b>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.510
<b>Haneda</b>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.510
<b>Yamamuro</b>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.510
<b>Kouda</b>

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.630
<i>Left field, Kouda-kun.</i>

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.510
<b>Miura</b>

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:41.490
<i>Center field, Yamamuro-kun.</i>

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.840
<i>Right field, Miura-kun.</i>

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:47.300
<i>Top of the first, Fuurin Academy to bat.</i>

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.760
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.760
<b>Fujii Chisato</b>

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.760
<i>Batting first, center field, Fujii-san.</i>

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.730
Play ball!

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:55.860
<i>Michiru-chan...</i>

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:02.150
Idemitsu, Seko, Uozumi, 
and Mayumura Jr., huh?

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.920
Our chances of beating them are zero.

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.980
You noticed 'em yet, Daigo?

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.680
Their unorthodox second
baseman and shortstop.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.370
Huh? What do you mean?

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:19.840
Strike!

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.550
Oh, man! I didn't spot that before.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.010
They're both lefties!

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.470
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.470
<b>Kabashima Anita</b>

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.470
It's true!

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:32.140
Strike two!

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:36.600
Huh? Wh-What? Is there something
wrong with playing lefties there?

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:41.570
Basically, the baseball playbook
says you don't play lefties there.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:42.520
Huh?

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:46.910
On second and third, and at shortstop,
a right-hander's throwing motion to first

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:50.190
is way, <i>way</i> faster than
a lefty's, so it's just logical.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:55.020
If you're left-handed, even securing
a difficult ball near second or third

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.810
requires you to turn your whole
body so you can throw to first,

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:00.460
which obviously takes longer.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.570
Now that you mention it...

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:04.670
Between short and third.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:10.430
Out!

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:11.890
She's fast!

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.830
How can she be that accurate while spinning?!

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.450
<i>I see now.</i>

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:22.340
<i>Even if you're left-handed, when you're as
good as that, it cancels out the downsides.</i>

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:26.820
<i>More importantly, they've got their
four best players up the middle.</i>

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.780
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.780
<b>Sagara Tao</b>

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:31.010
<i>Batting second, shortstop, Sagara-san.</i>

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.130
A drag bunt!

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:44.750
Out!

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:51.430
<i>It was a good idea to target the other fielders,
but they were ready for it.</i>

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:54.140
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:54.140
<b>Sawa Yayoi</b>

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.880
<i>Batting third, second base, Sawa-san.</i>

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:01.200
Out!

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.910
Three outs. Change sides!

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.210
You haven't lost your touch, Sawa.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.900
For girls, you and Tao have
got some killer baseball instincts.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:15.530
I knew you guys'd make the final.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:20.200
But this is as far as you get.
After all, we're here this year.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:31.510
Huh. That's pretty good. Is he Fuurin's ace?

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:35.220
Nope, he wears the number 9,
and he's not their ace, either.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.320
Their ace is out in right field.
She pitched yesterday and earlier.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.180
Hm, a girl, huh?

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.990
Well, she might be their ace,
but she's no Michiru.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:45.760
They only got this far by
being the least worst team.

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:48.740
Anyway, she won't pitch this game
because of pitch count restrictions.

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:52.400
So what pitches has that number 9 got?

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:53.800
Beats me.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:58.370
He might've pitched at some point,
but I left early, so I didn't see it.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:03.600
Well, whatever. We don't need
to go recon crazy at district level.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:07.840
You only need in-depth data when the
opposing team's actually worth scouting.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:12.050
<i>Bottom of the first, Oobi to bat.</i>

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:15.880
<i>Batting first, second base, Idemitsu-kun.</i>

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:14.760
Let's keep it tight!

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:17.760
Play!

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:22.920
Strike!

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:25.520
That's fast!

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.570
<i>Breaking balls are difficult.</i>

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:35.870
<i>With his control, we won't even 
be able to use them as decoys.</i>

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:41.340
Strike two!

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:47.150
Sorry, let's just give up on breaking balls.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:48.040
Huh?

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.340
These guys were strong
enough to beat Eihou.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:54.000
We're not gonna beat them with
a gimmick you barely practiced.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:09:00.030
Let's just come out firing and see
how far your fastballs can take us!

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.770
You're out.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.730
Hell yeah!

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.690
Nice one!

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:16.150
<i>Batting second, shortstop, Mayumura-san.</i>

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:23.480
What are you playing at?
Struck out in three pitches?

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:26.080
There's something weird about his pitches.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:31.000
Strike!

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:34.920
Strike two!

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:37.380
Not bad, wild punk.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:41.850
<i>So fast. It's obvious Nishina
was our ace-in-waiting all along.</i>

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.460
Strike! You're out!

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:55.550
All right! Nice pitchin'!

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:59.400
Come on now, what's wrong with you two?

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:03.240
We're in trouble. They're faster 
than they look from the sidelines.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:08.260
<i>Batting third, pitcher, Seko-kun.</i>

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:09.710
<i>Nice, Nishina.</i>

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:13.680
<i>He's throwing better than I expected,
and these pitches will do real damage.</i>

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:21.600
You're out! Change sides!

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.560
Hell yeah!

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.270
This is unexpected.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:31.230
Turns out there are some
live wires in rubber-ball.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:34.650
Looks like we're in for a fun game.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.400
Mifune Baseball Park

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.400
Mifune Baseball Park

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:41.450
Yikes, I'm super late!

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:42.200
Mifune Baseball Park

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:42.200
Mifune Baseball Park

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:46.160
The final's already started!

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:50.610
Crap, I'm crazy late.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:51.080
Mifune Baseball Park

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:51.080
Mifune Baseball Park

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:52.410
Wait... Fujii-kun?

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:54.290
Oh, hey, Kaoru-chan!

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:57.740
Why are you here? Come to cheer
on Mutsuko-chan and Daigo?

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:00.260
Well, that's one reason, but...

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:08.640
See the leadoff playing center field?

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
<b>Fuurin
Academy</b>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
<b>Fuurin
Academy</b>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
<b>Fujii</b>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
<b>Sagara</b>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
<b>Sawa</b>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
<b>Shigeno</b>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
<b>Nishina</b>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
<b>Kabashima</b>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
<b>Tanba</b>

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:10.850
That's our youngest!

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:14.850
Really?! Hm... Chisato-chan, wasn't it?

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:15.820
Yup.

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:18.800
Daigo didn't mention that.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:21.850
I reckon Daigo must've known...

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:24.910
Why didn't you tell me before?

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:28.320
I was planning on telling you when I saw you.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:31.160
Well, anyway, we'd better find a place to sit.

00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:34.990
Why so far back? Let's go down to the front.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:39.630
Daigo gets angry and embarrassed
whenever I show up to watch him.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.140
Ah, the wonders of puberty.

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:52.140
Out!

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:54.600
Unlucky.

00:11:58.930 --> 00:11:59.780
Dammit.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.520
Three outs! Change sides!

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.200
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.200
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.200
<b>Oobi</b>

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:10.270
Out!

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.750
Three outs! Change sides!

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:18.240
Hey, it's going all right.

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:18.710
<i>Sweet, we can match them!</i>

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:23.200
<i>Nishina's in great form, so if we can
just eke out a run and pull ahead...</i>

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.480
No!

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.590
<i>Uh, all right, maybe next inning.</i>

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:51.200
<i>Batting seventh, right field, Miura-kun.</i>

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.710
Strike! You're out!

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:01.980
Hell yeah!

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:05.400
Impressive. We haven't got a single hit yet.

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:09.100
What's more, everyone other
than Uozumi struck out.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.400
Well, there's no need to worry.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:14.940
He's pitching full speed against the bottom
of our order when it's not necessary.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:16.390
You're out!

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:23.570
He can't pitch in top gear forever.
He'll run out of steam soon.

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:25.410
Kouda!

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:31.660
Play!

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:34.830
What'd you just whisper to him, huh?!

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:36.790
Ball!

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.880
What did you tell him?

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:41.840
Oh, I just told him not to swing.

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:43.800
Ball!

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.600
Ball! Ball four!

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.230
Oh, boy.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.520
There goes his perfect game.

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:07.700
<i>Not good. He's starting to miss the zone more.</i>

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:10.620
Ball!

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:13.540
Ball!

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.440
Ball four!

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:23.960
T-Timeout!

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:25.790
Yikes.

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.770
He runs out of juice fast, this guy.

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:30.300
Pull it together, will ya?!

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:38.270
<i>We were aiming to nail them next inning,
but it looks like our chance has come early.</i>

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:44.190
<i>Batting second, shortstop, Mayumura-san.</i>

00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:55.540
<i>From two outs to consecutive walks,
with the top of the order at bat.</i>

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:59.250
<i>He went too hard and ran out
of gas after three innings.</i>

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:02.710
<i>We can probably score
three runs this inning.</i>

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:07.460
Strike!

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:11.430
<i>He's sacrificing his speed for more control?</i>

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:19.290
Your pitches got faster, but you don't have
the stamina to pitch a whole game yet.

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:24.400
And I was so in awe of your power,
I didn't think to warn you to take it easy

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.210
against their weaker
batters to pace yourself.

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:30.860
For now, we'll have to ease up on the
speed and focus on getting some strikes.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.630
Otherwise, we'll walk them to victory.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:36.840
They might connect with them,
but that doesn't mean guaranteed hits.

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:41.830
You've got seven teammates
behind you, backing you up.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:48.670
Right field!

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:51.130
<i>Damn, I got a bad connection.</i>

00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:54.090
Nice! Go get it, Mutsuko!

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:01.730
Okay! Run!

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:06.610
We took the lead!

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.600
Senpai, I got it!

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:09.570
I'm sorry!

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.030
That's two!

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:13.820
Stop, stop!

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:17.450
All right! Two runs ahead!

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:22.080
What was that about having
seven teammates behind me?

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:26.490
I'm sorry. I slipped on the wet grass.

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:28.630
Don't worry about it.

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:32.080
<i>Batting third, pitcher, Seko-kun.</i>

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:35.050
<i>We've had some luck, but it's going to plan so far.</i>

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:38.810
<i>You can't keep us four quiet
with that style of pitching.</i>

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:44.100
<i>Damn. If right field had got that one,
we woulda changed sides.</i>

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.020
To first!

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:52.240
Ou—

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.380
S-Safe!

00:16:53.380 --> 00:16:54.240
Safe!

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:57.200
All right! Three ahead!

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:01.120
I'm s-sorry.

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:03.080
T-Timeout!

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:07.780
We can't do anything about those
three runs. Let's put them behind us.

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:11.760
They made clean contact,
and our fielders are giving it their all, too.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:14.700
Anyway, their cleanup's dangerous,

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.720
so let's paint the corners,
and if we walk him, that's okay.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.430
Even with runners on first and second,
taking on their 5-hole and below

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:22.620
is way less risky.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:23.630
Right...

00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:28.900
Three runs, huh? I knew
we couldn't beat these guys.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:33.110
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Uozumi-kun.</i>

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:35.820
Feel free to kill 'em stone dead here!

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:42.410
<i>It's in the strike zone!</i>

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.210
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.210
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.210
<b>Oobi</b>

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:56.050
Two runs...

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:57.180
Oh, boy.

00:17:57.860 --> 00:17:59.140
It's 5-0.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:04.600
<i>I told him to paint the corners...</i>

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:08.290
<i>Nishina's already out of it mentally.</i>

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:12.320
<i>Batting fifth, third base, Hayazaka-kun.</i>

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:15.510
Five runs, huh? We got more than I expected.

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:17.970
Hey, Idemitsu, what are you doing?

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:18.840
Go to the bullpen.

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:19.460
Huh?

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:22.780
Don't worry so much.
My arm warms up in no time.

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:24.240
What?

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:30.350
Okay, okay. I hear ya.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:36.460
Hit by pitch!

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:39.580
Timeout!

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:44.770
Pull yourself together, Nishina!

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.260
It's the bottom of their order, 
and we only need one more out.

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:48.870
Sew this inning up already.

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.000
Switch me out.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:50.350
Huh?

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:52.810
It doesn't matter who takes over.

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:56.430
I don't wanna go through the motions
for a game that's already lost.

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:57.820
Switch me out already.

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:02.960
Are you done yet?

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:06.370
I won't do that.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:08.390
You <i>will</i> see this inning out!

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:14.750
Hey! What's <i>that</i> supposed to mean?!

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:15.920
Don't screw with me!

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.120
You tryna make me the scapegoat here?!

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:26.110
We don't have another pitcher ready!

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:29.500
Besides, the game isn't over yet, and
there's too many innings left to just give up!

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:32.770
A starting pitcher doesn't throw in the
towel just because they got a bloody nose!

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:36.680
What was that?

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:38.740
Wow, Daigo the Buddha just lost it!

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:40.740
Hm? Infighting?

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:44.770
<i>Batting sixth, first base, Haneda-kun.</i>

00:19:44.770 --> 00:19:45.700
Play!

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:52.160
<i>The hell? What's </i>he<i> getting pissed about?</i>

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:54.250
<i>I only asked to be switched out!</i>

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:56.750
Ball!

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:01.420
Ball!

00:20:10.260 --> 00:20:11.370
Strike!

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:19.400
Nice, nice!

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:22.110
Ball!

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.530
Nishina! You got this!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:34.580
Foul!

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:40.970
The game isn't over yet, and there's
too many innings left to just give up!

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:44.560
A starting pitcher doesn't throw in the
towel just because they got a bloody nose!

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:46.890
<i>You little twerp!</i>

00:20:57.130 --> 00:21:00.030
<i>Why am I the one being yelled at?</i>

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:03.050
<i>If you wanna yell at someone,
yell at those guys.</i>

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:10.700
<i>If those guys...</i>

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:17.520
<i>If those guys...</i>

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:21.670
<i>...hadn't dragged me down...</i>

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:25.380
<i>...we woulda changed sides already!</i>

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.350
Nice! That's going through!

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:13.180
Out!

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:16.710
Nice pitching.

00:22:16.710 --> 00:22:18.380
All right, let's shift gears and do this.

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:21.980
That was amazing, Senpai!

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:01.980
So 5-0, huh?

00:24:01.980 --> 00:24:04.090
This game's dead and buried, isn't it?

00:24:04.090 --> 00:24:07.170
Everybody seems to be hanging 
on for dear life, though.

00:24:07.170 --> 00:24:12.340
But their ace, Mayumura, will get up
on the mound at some point, right?

00:24:12.340 --> 00:24:14.460
There's no way we can hit her pitches.

00:24:14.460 --> 00:24:16.180
"No way," huh?

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:19.340
Hey, Tao. You sure you're okay with that?

00:24:19.340 --> 00:24:19.970
Huh?

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>Reconnected Feelings</b>

00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:22.590
Next time: "Reconnected Feelings."

00:24:22.590 --> 00:24:24.570
Run to the stage of your dreams!
